# Atlas — payroll vendors: effective-dated selection, shadow running, v2 payslips (Sprint 12)
# Login first (see auth.http) and paste the bearer token below.
# Prepare a payroll run first (see payroll.http) — shadow comparison runs against an existing run.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### The current vendor + switch history for a country (org admin / HR)
# With no assignments yet, "current" is AtlasNative (the default every org starts on).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/payroll/vendor-assignments?country=DEU
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Schedule a switch to LedgerPay for DEU, effective 1 August (org admin) → 201
# Effective-dated: a run created BEFORE this date keeps its old vendor (cycle-in-flight rule);
# a run created on/after it pins LedgerPay. The switch is a calendar decision, not an instant.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/payroll/vendor-assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "country": "DEU",
  "vendor": "LedgerPay",
  "effectiveFrom": "2026-08-01"
}

### An unknown vendor name → 400 (parsed to the enum at the edge; a typo never reaches the domain)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/payroll/vendor-assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "country": "DEU",
  "vendor": "LedgurPay",
  "effectiveFrom": "2026-08-01"
}

### A duplicate effective day → 422 (one assignment per country per effective day)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/payroll/vendor-assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "country": "DEU",
  "vendor": "AtlasNative",
  "effectiveFrom": "2026-08-01"
}

### The history now shows the scheduled switch, newest-effective first
GET {{host}}/api/v1/payroll/vendor-assignments?country=DEU
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Shadow-compare a prepared run against the pending vendor (org admin) → 201
# GATED: the org must be enrolled in the shadow programme (ShadowRunSettings) AND have a pending
# switch to trial. Un-enrolled or no-pending → 422. The report REDACTS net pay to deltas only.
# Paste a prepared run id from payroll.http.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/payroll/runs/PASTE_RUN_ID/shadow-compare
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The latest comparison report for a run (org admin / HR) — deltas + a divergence verdict, no salaries
GET {{host}}/api/v1/payroll/runs/PASTE_RUN_ID/shadow-comparison
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Shadow-compare when not enrolled / no pending switch → 422 (gated, or auto-expired after the flip)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/payroll/runs/PASTE_RUN_ID/shadow-compare
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ── API versioning: the same payslip, two shapes ────────────────────────────────────────────────

### v1 payslip — the flat, Kind-tagged line list, served UNCHANGED (byte-for-byte), now DEPRECATED
# Inspect the response headers: Deprecation, Sunset (RFC 8594), and Link rel="successor-version".
# Paste a payslip id from a prepared run (see payroll.http).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/payslips/PASTE_PAYSLIP_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### v2 payslip — the SAME data, lines GROUPED by kind (employeeDeductions / unpaidLeave / employerBurden)
# Same gross/net/employer-cost as v1; only the line structure evolved. No deprecation headers here.
GET {{host}}/api/v2/payslips/PASTE_PAYSLIP_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
